 <section id="q">
  <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">01</span><h2>Thesis &amp; the five classes</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">Agentic AI has spread across the origination pipeline and the collections/portfolio layer, but the credit-approval decision stays human-gated — because RBI’s explainability-and-accountability regime makes a black-box decision a compliance liability, not because the technology is missing. Fully autonomous lending exists only in small-ticket digital-native books (Trust Paisa) where a wrong call costs little.</p>
  <p>Everything in this dossier is sorted onto one spectrum, C0–C4, naming what each thing actually is regardless of the press release. Most published “AI use cases” are C0–C2; the honestly-agentic band is five use cases wide.</p>
  <div class="leg-grid"><article class="leg leg-c0"><div class="leg-top"><span class="leg-code">C0</span><div><h3>Deterministic automation</h3><p class="leg-era">1995–2010</p></div></div><p class="leg-what">Rule engines, RPA, API integration. No model, no learning.</p><p class="leg-tell"><span class="lbl">The tell</span>Drawable as a flowchart. CIBIL/GST pulls, penny-drop, CKYC, dedupe.</p><p class="leg-ag">Not AI at all</p></article>
<article class="leg leg-c1"><div class="leg-top"><span class="leg-code">C1</span><div><h3>Classical OCR / IDP</h3><p class="leg-era">OCR 20+ yrs; IDP ~2017</p></div></div><p class="leg-what">Template/zone OCR + ML extraction. Image → fields.</p><p class="leg-tell"><span class="lbl">The tell</span>Reads and extracts; does not reason. “AI KYC” usually sits here.</p><p class="leg-ag">Extraction, not agency</p></article>
<article class="leg leg-c2"><div class="leg-top"><span class="leg-code">C2</span><div><h3>Classical / predictive ML</h3><p class="leg-era">Scorecards 30+ yrs; ML ~2015</p></div></div><p class="leg-what">Scorecards, gradient boosting, anomaly, propensity. Narrow, single-task.</p><p class="leg-tell"><span class="lbl">The tell</span>Outputs a number or class. Predicts; does not converse or plan.</p><p class="leg-ag">Real AI — the OLD AI</p></article>
<article class="leg leg-c3"><div class="leg-top"><span class="leg-code">C3</span><div><h3>Generative AI (non-agentic)</h3><p class="leg-era">2023+</p></div></div><p class="leg-what">LLM doing ONE task a human triggers and consumes.</p><p class="leg-tell"><span class="lbl">The tell</span>Human presses go, human uses output. No self-directed action.</p><p class="leg-ag">New, but not agentic</p></article>
<article class="leg leg-c4"><div class="leg-top"><span class="leg-code">C4</span><div><h3>Agentic AI</h3><p class="leg-era">2024+ (nascent)</p></div></div><p class="leg-what">LLM + planning + tools + memory. Plans, calls APIs, loops, executes.</p><p class="leg-tell"><span class="lbl">The tell</span>Decides what to do next and does it, across a file or portfolio.</p><p class="leg-ag">Yes — the orchestration only</p></article></div>
 </section>

