 <section id="buildwait">
  <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">06</span><h2>Build vs wait — the HFS call</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">Five honestly-agentic bets. One build, two splits, two waits — with cost anchors, timelines, KPIs, and the trigger that flips each verdict. “Wait” mostly means: buy the mature non-agentic slice now.</p>
  <div class="assume"><h4>Assumptions — recalibrate if wrong</h4><p>HFS as an emerging NBFC consolidating lending-tech foundations; volumes well below L&amp;T/Bajaj; vendor-led delivery; FREE-AI applying in full. Cost ranges are directional market anchors, not quotes.</p></div>
  <div class="summary"><div class="sm sm-build"><span class="sm-v">Build now</span><span class="sm-n">Portfolio-monitoring co-pilot</span></div><div class="sm sm-split"><span class="sm-v">Split</span><span class="sm-n">Agentic self-service resolution</span></div><div class="sm sm-split"><span class="sm-v">Split</span><span class="sm-n">Agentic collections orchestration</span></div><div class="sm sm-wait"><span class="sm-v">Wait</span><span class="sm-n">Agentic underwriting co-pilot</span></div><div class="sm sm-wait"><span class="sm-v">Wait</span><span class="sm-n">Agentic compliance file check</span></div></div>
  <div class="crit-grid"><div class="crit"><span class="crit-n">01</span><div><h4>RBI constraint height</h4><p>Heavier accountability/explainability burden → keep the human in the loop, wait.</p></div></div>
<div class="crit"><span class="crit-n">02</span><div><h4>Market maturity</h4><p>In production at named peers = safe to buy. Claimed/piloted = don’t be the guinea pig.</p></div></div>
<div class="crit"><span class="crit-n">03</span><div><h4>Build economics</h4><p>HFS volumes don’t amortise bespoke agentic builds. Default: buy or partner.</p></div></div>
<div class="crit"><span class="crit-n">04</span><div><h4>Value to a growing book</h4><p>Risk visibility and cost-to-serve pay off before a faster credit memo.</p></div></div>
<div class="crit"><span class="crit-n">05</span><div><h4>Downside asymmetry</h4><p>A conduct/compliance incident is near-existential for a young lender.</p></div></div>
<div class="crit"><span class="crit-n">06</span><div><h4>Foundations readiness</h4><p>Clean data, reason codes, audit logs, drift monitoring — the FREE-AI list is the C4 gate.</p></div></div></div>
  <article class="card" id="bw-portfolio"><div class="card-head"><div class="card-title"><h3>Portfolio-monitoring co-pilot</h3><p class="csub">NL query over delinquency/vintage data; flags stress, recommends action; human acts.</p></div><span class="vbadge v-build">Build now</span></div><div class="card-meta"><span class="chip chip-C4">C4</span> <span class="mat mat-production">In production</span> <span class="mtag">RBI: Medium</span> <span class="mtag">Peers: L&amp;T Orion / Nostradamus</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">₹40–80L build (2–3 engineers + LLM API) or ₹8–20L/yr SaaS</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">90-day v1 feasible</span></div><div class="gauge"><div class="track"><span class="stop" style="left:12%">Wait</span><span class="stop" style="left:37%">Pilot</span><span class="stop" style="left:62%">Buy</span><span class="stop" style="left:87%">Build</span><div class="fill fill-build" style="width:85%"></div><div class="dot dot-build" style="left:85%"></div></div></div><div class="fw"><div class="fw-col fw-build"><h4>Case to build</h4><ul><li>Lowest regulatory friction — internal, human acts on output.</li><li>Highest survival value for a scaling book: early, granular risk visibility.</li><li>Rides on data + EWS you must build anyway.</li><li>Safe place to learn agentic orchestration.</li></ul></div><div class="fw-col fw-wait"><h4>Case to wait</h4><ul><li>Needs a consolidated data lake and working EWS underneath, or the agent surfaces noise.</li></ul></div></div><div class="hfs"><span class="hfs-lbl">HFS call</span><p><strong>Green-light.</strong> NL-query + threshold alerting over portfolio data on/alongside a C2 EWS. Wrong output costs a second look, not a customer.</p><div class="moves"><div><span class="mv">First move</span>90-day v1: NL queries + alerts on one product’s book.</div><div><span class="mv">Escalate when</span>— start now.</div><div><span class="mv">KPIs to run</span>Query adoption by risk team; % of EWS flags actioned <7 days; false-alert rate</div></div></div></article>
<article class="card" id="bw-servicing"><div class="card-head"><div class="card-title"><h3>Agentic self-service resolution</h3><p class="csub">Agent fetches account, executes the change, confirms — end-to-end.</p></div><span class="vbadge v-split">Split — C3 now, agentic later</span></div><div class="card-meta"><span class="chip chip-C4">C4</span> <span class="mat mat-piloted">Piloted</span> <span class="mtag">RBI: Highest</span> <span class="mtag">Peers: Bajaj (800→600)</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">C3 assistant: ₹10–25L/yr SaaS. Agentic layer: defer</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">C3 live in 60–90 days</span></div><div class="gauge"><div class="track"><span class="stop" style="left:12%">Wait</span><span class="stop" style="left:37%">Pilot</span><span class="stop" style="left:62%">Buy</span><span class="stop" style="left:87%">Build</span><div class="fill fill-split" style="width:37%"></div><div class="dot dot-split" style="left:37%"></div></div></div><div class="fw"><div class="fw-col fw-build"><h4>Case to build</h4><ul><li>Deflects servicing cost; 24×7 coverage as the base grows.</li></ul></div><div class="fw-col fw-wait"><h4>Case to wait</h4><ul><li>The agentic increment = autonomous state changes — action-risk and grievance exposure out of proportion to a small book.</li><li>Unproven even at Bajaj scale.</li></ul></div></div><div class="hfs"><span class="hfs-lbl">HFS call</span><p>Buy a <strong>C3 assistant now</strong> (FAQs, statements, status — no state changes): ~80% of value at ~20% of risk. Hold execution until guardrails and peer proof mature.</p><div class="moves"><div><span class="mv">First move</span>C3 assistant on top-20 query intents.</div><div><span class="mv">Escalate when</span>Contained-resolution plateaus + provable execution guardrails.</div><div><span class="mv">KPIs to run</span>Containment rate; CSAT on bot sessions; escalation accuracy; cost per resolved query</div></div></div></article>
<article class="card" id="bw-collections"><div class="card-head"><div class="card-title"><h3>Agentic collections orchestration</h3><p class="csub">Agent decides + executes across the account — message, call, escalate, log.</p></div><span class="vbadge v-split">Split — C2/C3 now, agentic later</span></div><div class="card-meta"><span class="chip chip-C4">C4</span> <span class="mat mat-piloted">Piloted</span> <span class="mtag">RBI: Highest</span> <span class="mtag">Peers: emerging</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">Propensity + reminder bot: ₹15–35L/yr vendor stack</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">Propensity 60 days; bot 90 days</span></div><div class="gauge"><div class="track"><span class="stop" style="left:12%">Wait</span><span class="stop" style="left:37%">Pilot</span><span class="stop" style="left:62%">Buy</span><span class="stop" style="left:87%">Build</span><div class="fill fill-split" style="width:30%"></div><div class="dot dot-split" style="left:30%"></div></div></div><div class="fw"><div class="fw-col fw-build"><h4>Case to build</h4><ul><li>High-ROI function; orchestration promises timing/channel optimisation.</li></ul></div><div class="fw-col fw-wait"><h4>Case to wait</h4><ul><li>Highest-conduct-risk zone — recovery rules, grievance redressal, Digital Lending MD amendments all bite here.</li><li>One conduct incident = asymmetric damage for a young lender.</li><li>Autonomous layer unproven.</li></ul></div></div><div class="hfs"><span class="hfs-lbl">HFS call</span><p>Buy <strong>C2 propensity prioritisation</strong> + <strong>C3 multilingual reminder bots</strong> (script-bounded). Wait on autonomy until kill-switches and clean peer conduct outcomes exist.</p><div class="moves"><div><span class="mv">First move</span>Propensity bucketing + bounded reminder bot.</div><div><span class="mv">Escalate when</span>Provable conduct guardrails + peer conduct evidence.</div><div><span class="mv">KPIs to run</span>Roll-back rate by bucket; promise-to-pay kept %; complaints per 10k contacts (watch this one)</div></div></div></article>
<article class="card" id="bw-underwriting"><div class="card-head"><div class="card-title"><h3>Agentic underwriting co-pilot</h3><p class="csub">Ingest → bureau → spread → memo → route, around a human underwriter.</p></div><span class="vbadge v-wait">Wait — foundations first</span></div><div class="card-meta"><span class="chip chip-C4">C4</span> <span class="mat mat-production">In production</span> <span class="mtag">RBI: Highest</span> <span class="mtag">Peers: L&amp;T Helios · Tata</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">Bespoke: ₹2–5cr — doesn’t amortise. Vendor pilot later: ₹30–60L</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">Revisit in 12–18 months</span></div><div class="gauge"><div class="track"><span class="stop" style="left:12%">Wait</span><span class="stop" style="left:37%">Pilot</span><span class="stop" style="left:62%">Buy</span><span class="stop" style="left:87%">Build</span><div class="fill fill-wait" style="width:22%"></div><div class="dot dot-wait" style="left:22%"></div></div></div><div class="fw"><div class="fw-col fw-build"><h4>Case to build</h4><ul><li>Peers report ~30% TAT cut, 1.5 hrs/SME case saved.</li><li>Keeps scarce underwriters on judgment.</li></ul></div><div class="fw-col fw-wait"><h4>Case to wait</h4><ul><li>Needs mature LOS/LMS, clean spreading, live reason-code + audit layer.</li><li>HFS volumes don’t amortise a bespoke multi-agent build.</li><li>RBI keeps the human on the decision — payoff caps at “faster human.”</li><li>LOS vendors will ship this as a feature within 12–18 months.</li></ul></div></div><div class="hfs"><span class="hfs-lbl">HFS call</span><p>Don’t build. Fix C0–C2 foundations + reason-code/audit layer (needed for FREE-AI anyway). Then run a <em>narrow bought pilot</em> on one product line.</p><div class="moves"><div><span class="mv">First move</span>Foundations inventory + explicit volume trigger.</div><div><span class="mv">Escalate when</span>Volume + clean data amortise a co-pilot; vendor offers FREE-AI-aligned explainability.</div><div><span class="mv">KPIs to run</span>(pre-work) % files with complete digital data; reason-code coverage; TAT baseline</div></div></div></article>
<article class="card" id="bw-compliance"><div class="card-head"><div class="card-title"><h3>Agentic compliance file check</h3><p class="csub">Agent checks each file vs policy, flags gaps, files exceptions autonomously.</p></div><span class="vbadge v-wait">Wait — immature</span></div><div class="card-meta"><span class="chip chip-C4">C4</span> <span class="mat mat-claimed">Claimed</span> <span class="mtag">RBI: Highest</span> <span class="mtag">Peers: rarely mature</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">C3 RAG assistant: ₹5–15L. Agentic: no credible vendor</span><span class="mtag mtag-cost">RAG in 45–60 days</span></div><div class="gauge"><div class="track"><span class="stop" style="left:12%">Wait</span><span class="stop" style="left:37%">Pilot</span><span class="stop" style="left:62%">Buy</span><span class="stop" style="left:87%">Build</span><div class="fill fill-wait" style="width:10%"></div><div class="dot dot-wait" style="left:10%"></div></div></div><div class="fw"><div class="fw-col fw-build"><h4>Case to build</h4><ul><li>Appealing on paper — policy conformance on every file.</li></ul></div><div class="fw-col fw-wait"><h4>Case to wait</h4><ul><li>Mostly vaporware; few audited deployments anywhere.</li><li>A young NBFC should not be the guinea pig for autonomous compliance.</li></ul></div></div><div class="hfs"><span class="hfs-lbl">HFS call</span><p>Deploy a <strong>C3 RAG policy/circular assistant</strong> for the compliance team. Hold the agentic file-check; monitor the market.</p><div class="moves"><div><span class="mv">First move</span>RAG over internal policy + RBI circulars.</div><div><span class="mv">Escalate when</span>≥2 credible vendors with audited in-production deployments.</div><div><span class="mv">KPIs to run</span>Compliance-team query volume; answer-accuracy sampling; time saved per policy lookup</div></div></div></article>
