<tr><td class="fa-item">Customer-facing AI disclosure + grievance path</td><td class="fa-ev">Bot scripts + grievance SLA</td><td class="fa-own">Customer Service Head</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
 </section>

 <section id="bottom">
  <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Bottom line</h2></div>
  <div class="bl">
   <div class="kicker">One paragraph to defend in any room</div>
   <h2 style="font-size:1.45rem;margin:0 0 14px">The pipeline is agentic. The decision is human. The gate is foundations.</h2>
   <p>Agentic AI is real in Indian lending’s pipeline, servicing and portfolio layers, and absent from the credit decision — by regulation, not by technology gap. For HFS: build one agent now (portfolio monitoring, ~90 days), buy the mature C2/C3 slices of servicing and collections, wait on underwriting (12–18 months, then a bought pilot) and agentic compliance (vendor market immature). Spend the difference on the FREE-AI checklist — reason codes, audit logs, drift monitoring, board policy — because it is both the compliance requirement and the precondition for every future agent. Re-run the five verdicts each quarter against peer disclosures; the trigger conditions are written on each card.</p>
  </div>
 </section>

